return {
["12:00"]={"Dismount and use your footwork, your circles, your angles and your science; for I intend to make you see stars at \003noon\004 with my modern, uncouth skill","Don Quixote","Miguel de Cervantes"},
["12:01"]={"“Madam President …” Florentyna had to think quickly to prevent anyone noticing her instinctive response to the words. “It’s \003one minute past midday\004.”","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:02"]={"At \003two minutes past twelve\004 the door opens and two men come into the lobby. One is tall with black hair combed in a 50’s pompadour. The other is short and bespectacled. Both are wearing suits.","Billy Summers","Stephen King"},
["12:03"]={"It was now \003three minutes after midday\004. The blinds had been earlier drawn down, seeming to disconnect time as well as shutting out the surly half-light of late morning.","The Murder Room","P.D. James"},
["12:04"]={"I wake up the next day seized by panic. I bolt out of bed and stumble into the kitchen where I look at the clock on the microwave: \00312:04 P.M.\004","Dry: A Memoir","Augusten Boroughs"},
["12:06"]={"A few minutes’ light \003around noon\004 is all that you need to discover the error, and re-set the clock – provide that you bother to go up and make the observation.","Odalisque: The Baroque Cycle #3","Neal Stephenson"},
["12:07"]={"On a Monday Simon Hirsch was going to break his leg at \003seven minutes after 12\004, noon, and as soon as Satan told us the day before, Seppi went to betting with me that it would not happen, and soon they got excited and went to betting with me themselves.","The Chronicle of Young Satan","Mark Twain"},
["12:08"]={"When a clock struck noon in Washington, D.C., the time was \00312:08\004 in Philadelphia, 12:12 in New York, and 12:24 in Boston.","Eighty Days","Matthew Goodman"},
["12:10"]={"The child said that it was \003twelve-ten\004 and that Gonda was already late. Another child said that maybe the rain had delayed him. Another said, no not the rain, his director was taking a plane from Hollywood.","Enoch and the Gorilla","Flannery O’Connor"},
["12:11"]={"She was to leave the reception as soon as she could and return to her room to change clothes. At \00312:11\004 there’d be another blackout, during which she’d take the outside stairwell to the ground floor and wait at the exit for a Broadmoor’s catering van.","The Enclave","Karen Hancock"},
["12:12"]={"Were you on Carlin Street at approximately \00312:12\004 when Carietta White came out of the First Congregational Church on that street?","Carrie","Stephen King"},
["12:13"]={"It’s \00312:13\004, so it can be lunch. My favorite bit of the prayer is the daily bread. I’m the boss of play, but Ma’s the boss of meals, like she doesn’t let us have cereal for breakfast and lunch and dinner in case we’d get sick and anyway that would use it up too fast.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["12:14"]={"She left London on the \003twelve-fourteen\004 from Paddington, arriving at Bristol (where she had to change) at two-fifty.","The Plymouth Express","Agatha Christie"},
["12:15"]={"What shall I think of that’s liberating and refreshing? I’m in the mood when I open my window at night and look at the stars. Unfortunately it’s \00312:15\004 on a grey dull day, the aeroplanes are active","A Writer’s Diary: Being Extracts from the Diary of Virgina Woolf","Virginia Woolf"},
["12:16"]={"At \00312:16\004 Miss Glory brought out the food. It took me a week to learn the difference between a salad plate,a bread plate and a dessert plate.","I Know Why the Caged Bird Sings","Maya Angelou"},
["12:17"]={"Kava ordered two glasses of coffee for himself and his beloved and some cake. When the pair left, exactly \003seventeen minutes after twelve\004, the club began to buzz with excitement.","Vanvild Kava","Isaac Bashevis Singer"},
["12:19"]={"Not believed to have slept in her bed last night. Could not have left island due to blocked bridge. None of family members has any knowledge as to HV’s whereabouts. At \00312:19 p.m.\004: G.M. informed by telephone about the situation.","The Girl With the Dragon Tattoo","Stieg Larsson"},
["12:20"]={"It was already \00312:20 p.m.\004, and he hadn’t heard a word from Fisher, despite giving him clear instructions to call the moment the meeting was over.","Be Careful What You Wish For","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:21"]={"\00312:21 GMT\004\n“Any questions?” asked Jackie when she’d come to the end of her briefing.\nA hand shot up. “Which of the two teams is more likely to be needed?”","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:22"]={"By \003twenty-two minutes past twelve\004 we leave, much too soon for our desires, this delightful spot, where the pilgrims are in the habit of bathing who come to visit the Jordan.","Narrative of a Journey Round the Dead Sea and in the Bible Lands in 1850 and 1851","Félicien de Saulcy"},
["12:23"]={"It would feel, she realised, altogether too strange to climb into the same bed with a man she hadn’t seen for two years.\nShe noticed the time on the digital alarm clock. \00312:23\004.","The Midnight Library","Matt Haig"},
["12:25"]={"\00312:25 pm\004. 26. 27. Every time Billy saved a shot he looked heartbroken.","A Kestrel for a Knave","Barry Hines"},
["12:26"]={"\00312:26 P.M.\004\n“I, Florentyna Kane, do solemnly swear …”\n“I, Florentyna Kane, do solemnly swear …”","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:27"]={"For three decades, time had been frozen at \003twelve twenty-seven\004. The story was that the hands had stopped at the exact moment Corcoran O’Connor’s father died. It might have been true.","Boundary Waters","William Kent Krueger"},
["12:28"]={"The DRINK CHEER-UP COFFEE wall clock read \00312:28\004.","11/22/63","Stephen King"},
["12:29"]={"“What time is it?” asked Teeny-bits.\nThe station agent hauled out his big silver watch, looked at it critically and announced: “\003Twenty-nine minutes past twelve\004.”\n“Past twelve!” repeated Teeny-bits. “It can’t be.”","The Mark of the Knife","Clayton H. Ernst"},
["12:30"]={"You’ll never believe this but (in Spain) they are two hours late for ever meal — two hours Fanny — (can we lunch at \003half-past twelve\004 today?)","Love in a Cold Climate","Nancy Mitford"},
["12:31"]={"WELCOME TO TEXAS. IT IS NINETY-ONE DEGREES OUTSIDE WITH NO WIND. THE TIME IS \00312:31 P.M.\004 WE HOPE THAT YOU’VE ENJOYED YOUR FLIGHT AND THANKS FOR FLYING AMERICAN AIRLINES.","Dark Obsession","William B. Lyons"},
["12:32"]={"A chutney-biting brigadier named Boyd-Boyd fixed an appointment on the phone with Oxted, at Hornborough Station, for the \003twelve thirty-two\004. He was to deliver the goods.","Extremely Entertaining Short Stories","Stacy Aumonier"},
["12:33"]={"Stephen Maxie looked him straight in the eye and said almost casually: “It was \003thirty-three minutes past twelve\004 by my watch.”","Cover Her Face","P.D. James"},
["12:36"]={"\00312:36 CET\004\nOnce the ship had docked, William and Monti leaned over the railing and watched as Grant lugged the casket down the gangway. He was still clutching it as he climbed into the back seat of a waiting car.","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:37"]={"It was \00312:37\004 when Jason, in blue jeans, cap and dark, tattered V-necked sweater, reached the gates of the old factory. He took out a pack of Gauloise cigarettes and leaned against the wall, lighting one with a match, holding the flame longer than necessary before he blew it out.","The Bourne Ultimatum","Robert Ludlum"},
["12:40"]={"When it came to work, Anne was always on time, and at \00312:40 P.M.\004 she appeared from the Piccadilly end of the street.","Not a Penny More, Not a Penny Less","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:41"]={"At \00312:41\004 President-elect and Mrs. Tucker finally embarked in their limousine. He instructed me to work with Feeley on a speech insert explaining the delay.","The White House Mess","Christopher Buckley"},
["12:43"]={"Died five minutes ago, you say? he asked. His eye went to the watch on his wrist. \003Twelve-forty-three\004, he wrote on the blotter.","A Pocket Full of Rye","Agatha Christie"},
["12:44"]={"A few minutes later they were crossing the bridge over the Arizona Canal. Matt pulled out his old silver watch.\n“Only \003sixteen minutes to one\004,” he announced, with a note of exultation, “and we’re fifteen miles on our way.”","Motor Matt’s Century Run","Stanley R. Matthews"},
["12:45"]={"On Friday at \00312:45 P.M.\004, David arrived at the Athenaeum, a massive white building on the corner of Pall Mall, overlooked by a statue of the Duke of York.","Not a Penny More, Not a Penny Less","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:46"]={"It is \003around quarter to one\004. No sunlight comes into the room now through the windows at right. Outside the day is fine but increasingly sultry, with a faint haziness in the air which softens the glare of the sun.","Long Day’s Journey Into Night","Eugene O’Neill"},
["12:47"]={"At \003forty-seven minutes past twelve\004 they reached the buoy, it was in perfect condition, and must have shifted but little.","Around the Moon","Jules Verne"},
["12:48"]={"Scarcely had we left the golf links behind than he remarked — until that moment he had not uttered a single word, nor had I — “If you’re going by the \00312:48\004 I’ll see you off.”","Under One Flag","Richard Marsh"},
["12:49"]={"The first victim of the Krefeld raid died at \00312:49 hours\004 Double British Summer Time at B Flight, but it wasn’t due to carelessness.","Bomber","Len Deighton"},
["12:50"]={"He checked his watch: \00312:50\004. They still had more than enough time to reach the top and be back in their little tent before the last rays of sunlight disappeared.","Paths of Glory","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:51"]={"At \00312:51\004 James Burdick came on the air again. The material for exchange will shortly arrive and we need your permission for the aircraft to land. Zade gave it.","The Kobra Manifesto","Adam Hall"},
["12:52"]={"Consuela stood on the pavement and checked her watch. It was \00312:52\004, and she had to accept that it had been a fruitless morning.","Cheap at Half the Price","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:53"]={"Aboot twelve miles. We ought tae pass her at Pinmore. She’s due there at \00312:53\004.","Five Red Herrings","Dorothy L. Sayers"},
["12:55"]={"But when Curry rose at \003five minutes to one\004 to introduce item Three, there was a sharp revival of interest. It was called, “Rectification of an Anomaly of the Stipends of Junior Fellows.”","That Hideous Strength","C.S. Lewis"},
["12:56"]={"If he was ignored till one o’clock, he promised himself, he would leave. He watched the filigreed minute hand jerk from five minutes to \003four minutes to one\004.","Sharpe’s Revenge","Bernard Cornwell"},
["12:57"]={"Monday, April 6\n\00312:57 P.M.\004\nStone Aimes was floating through cyberspace, through the massive data pages of the National Institutes of Health. Since the Gerex Corporation had a complete clampdown on their clinical-trial results, he was attempting an end run.","Syndrome","Thomas Hoover"},
["12:58"]={"At \003two minutes to one\004, Charlie Duncan entered the Palm Court restaurant wearing an open-necked shirt and smoking a cigarette—a walking H. M. Bateman cartoon.","A Prisoner of Birth","Jeffrey Archer"},
["12:59"]={"We need the Holy Spirit. It’s almost Advent. We await. Please help. Amen.\nStephen checked the time. It was \00312:59 PM\004.","An Advent for Religious Liberty","Ray Keating"},
}
